12. SCCM / ConfigMgr NAA exposure
ATSB recovered cached SCCM Network Access Account secrets.     ATSB SOE Penetration Test Repor…
First determine whether ConfigMgr exists:
Get-Service CcmExec -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

Test-Path "C:\Windows\CCM"
Test-Path "C:\Windows\CCMSetup"

Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\ccm -ClassName SMS_Client -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

Check relevant files/directories that are readable:
Get-ChildItem C:\Windows\CCM -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
Select-Object Name,FullName

And installed product:
Get-CimInstance Win32_Product -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
Where-Object {$_.Name -match 'Configuration Manager|SCCM'}

I would stop at identifying whether NAA/policy credential material is exposed to the standard user. We do not need to decrypt real account credentials unless the ROE explicitly calls for that.
Finding: sensitive SCCM credential material readable by a standard user.
